    "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\nThe NanoV3 GB200 EP4 benchmark completes successfully but repeatedly exceeds the +20% throughput improvement ceiling at batch 128. Refresh its stale performance reference from the complete median-throughput row of three fresh GB200 sweeps and restore the recipe's original `mr` scope, which was quarantined in #7916.\n\nBatch-128 throughput changes from **11,512.760738** to **14,234.332897 tokens/sec**. Update its throughput, average/p50/p99 latency, and TPOT together using the original full-precision result. Retain the existing 10% regression tolerance, 20% throughput improvement ceiling, other batch references, and benchmark metadata. Restoring `scope: [mr]` returns the pre-quarantine GitLab selection.\n\n### Validation\n\nThree independent server launches on two GB200 nodes reproduced the same isolated high-side failure against the original reference. Each sweep ran batch sizes 1, 8, 32, and 128 with five warmups and ten timed iterations per batch.\n\n| Sweep | Batch-128 throughput (tok/s) | Change vs old baseline | Average latency (ms) | p99 latency (ms) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | 14,218.683365 | +23.50% | 1,137.180562 | 1,209.695876 |\n| 2 | 14,248.113662 | +23.76% | 1,134.807123 | 1,193.082603 |\n| 3 — selected median throughput | 14,234.332897 | +23.64% | 1,136.289481 | 1,236.761791 |\n\nThe selected baseline is the complete batch-128 row from sweep 3, not a mixture of independently selected metric values. The sample throughput coefficient of variation is 0.103%.\n\nRuntime provenance: source `d7157825675a65c2503a061ffd1fffa7886df9b7`; CI image tag `main_73361945` (PyTorch 26.09); ARM64 manifest `sha256:5f37d7e0464e5abab9ec8b22f808d11a81bb23a859f9dfd99a1e4e2d49b98f71`. The runs used four GB200 GPUs, TP=1/PP=1/EP=4, FlashAttention 2, legacy scheduling, NVLS dispatch, GSM8K prompts, and 128 output tokens. W&B upload was disabled. Runtime arguments confirm the same checkpoint and principal model configuration as the historical run.\n\n- The original reference fails exactly one of 20 comparisons in each fresh sweep: batch-128 throughput.\n- Replaying the official comparator with the refreshed reference passes **all 60 metric comparisons** across the three fresh sweeps.\n- Four archived runs with isolated high-throughput failures also pass after refresh. The two archived runs with p99 latency outliers continue to fail.\n- Verified finite measurements, matching batch-128 metadata, exact provenance of the adopted full-precision row, and preserved values in other batch rows.\n- JSON/YAML validation and `git diff --check` pass. Ran `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh`; it found no changed Python files to format.\n\nThis is direct GPU benchmark execution followed by comparator replay. Full CI on the PR head is pending. The separate historical p99 outliers remain unresolved, and three sweeps do not establish a fleet-wide flake rate. The source/dependency change responsible for the underlying speedup has not been bisected.\n\n:warning: For major changes (either in lines of code or in its impact), please make sure to first share a design doc with the team. If you're unsure what's the best way to do so, contact @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nFor PRs from open-source community contributors:\n\n- **New features**: a linked issue is **required**. Please open a [feature request](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/issues/new?template=feature_request.md) and reference it here before submitting the PR.\n- **Small updates (bug fixes, minor improvements)**: a linked issue is **recommended** and will accelerate the PR review process.\n\nLinked issue: [MCORE-861](https://linear.app/nvidia/issue/MCORE-861/nanov3-gb200-batch128-throughput-2239percent-exceeds-20percent) — addresses the NanoV3 batch-128 throughput-ceiling failure. The separately grouped GPT16B alert is outside this change.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [ ] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel (Triton, `jit_fuser`/`torch.compile`, CUDA extension, TE or external-library dispatch, or a scatter/index accumulation), I have added or updated its bit-exact determinism test and registered it in `tests/unit_tests/determinism/kernels/manifest.py` ([guide](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/docs/developer/determinism/testing.md))\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [x] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n\nThe existing performance recipe supplies the functional coverage; this change adds no Python code, GPU kernels, typing interfaces, or new test files. The personal-review attestation above remains for the human PR author.\n\n### Code review\n\nFeel free to message or comment @NVIDIA/mcore-oncall to help accelerate your merge into main. The less complex your PR is, the faster it will be approved and merged!\n\nAll PRs start as **draft**. If you open a non-draft PR, it will be automatically converted to draft.\n\n#### Step 1: Mark PR as \"Ready for Review\"\n\n1. When your PR is ready, click **Ready for Review**.\n2. An oncall reviewer is auto-assigned and expert reviewers are notified based on your changes.\n   - Some PRs may jump straight to step 2. This is determined by `.github/CODEOWNERS`.\n\n:warning: Only mark as ready once merge-conflicts are resolved and the CI is passing.\nFinal Review might get declined if these requirements are not fulfilled.\n\n#### Step 2: Final Review\n\nFor PRs that change `megatron/core`, once all expert reviewers have approved, the `Final Review` label is applied **automatically** and final reviewers are assigned.\n\nFor PRs outside `megatron/core`, this step is skipped.\n\n#### Step 3: Approved\n\nOnce all required reviewers have approved, the `Approved` label is applied **automatically**.\n\n### Merge\n\nAny member of [mcore-engineers](https://github.com/orgs/NVIDIA/teams/mcore-engineers) will be able to merge your PR.\n",
